# tests/fixtures/ IS tracked on purpose (the eval set and SERP captures are how
# scoring gets tuned), but it holds real people's public profile data — keep
# this repository private, and see the guardrails section of README.md before
# pushing it anywhere.

# The job search's personal answers — work authorisation, skills. The tracked
# *.example.yaml files are what loads until these exist.
config/job_search.yaml
config/my_skills.yaml
config/my_profile.md

# ── the CV / cover-letter engine ──
# Per-run intermediates: analyses, drafts, rejected letters, trace.jsonl.
# `run/*` rather than `run/`: git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so ignoring the contents is what makes the exception below work.
run/*
# …except the voice ratings. That file is the only record of whether the letters
# are getting better, the scores in it are Simon's own, and a `run/` clean would
# otherwise throw away every round of the loop.
!run/voice_eval.csv
# Generated applications. Personal, and regenerable from profile/ + the job id.
output/
